## Context

Observed 2026-09-30 on padme: the DVC remote of this repository
(`/data/projets/dvc/oeconomia-climate-finance`, `.dvc/config.local`) and the
working DVC cache under `/home/haduong` are two btrfs subvolumes (`@data`,
`@home_haduong`) of the same partition, `/dev/nvme1n1p2`. The DVC
configuration names no other remote. The archived snapshots of JETP
documents (`data/jetp/documents.dvc`) therefore exist on one physical drive;
some of those pages have since disappeared from the web, so a drive failure
would lose evidence the M3 release is built from.

Not established: whether padme has a machine-level backup outside DVC. Only
the DVC configuration was inspected; the author knows.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The author states whether a machine-level backup of padme's `/data` exists, and where
- [ ] If none: the document bytes have a copy on another physical device or site (the operation spec draft proposes doudou pulling a copy after each push; an institutional or cloud store is an alternative), and a restore of one snapshot from it is tested
- [ ] `docs/jetp-operation.md` (backups section) states the arrangement
